digraph account_payable_process_175 {
	graph [rankdir=LR]
	START_NODE [label="" shape=circle width=0.3]
	subgraph CLUSTER_0 {
		"send to the vendor accounting department" [shape=box]
		"create a receiving report" [shape=box]
		"send to the vendor accounting department" -> "create a receiving report"
		"double check a three-way match" [shape=box]
		"create a receiving report" -> "double check a three-way match"
		"schedule the payment" [shape=box]
		"double check a three-way match" -> "schedule the payment"
	}
	START_NODE -> "send to the vendor accounting department"
	END_NODE [label="" shape=doublecircle width=0.2]
	"schedule the payment" -> END_NODE
	fontsize=15 label="\n\n
The text below is about the account payable process. It starts with sending to the vendor accounting department. 
When sending to the vendor accounting department is completed, you need to create a receiving report.
When creating a receiving report is completed, you need to double check a three-way match.
After doubling check a three-way match, you need to schedule the payment.
The process is now completed. 
"
	fontsize=15 label="\n\n
The text below is about the account payable process: it starts with sending to vendor accounting department.
When the processing of sending to the vendor accounting department is completed, you need to create a receipt report.
When a receiving report is completed you must check a three-way match twice.
After doubling a three-way match, you need to schedule the payment.
The process is now complete.
"
}
